Result
SceneDB is now the sole persistent authority for scene components and subsystems.
#[gpu] fields use component-local, stable GPU partner rows with DirtyTracked or explicit Once semantics.
Helio owns only compact projections, temporal history, culling outputs, render caches, residency metadata, and pass-derived buffers.
Geometry uses the explicit named Once handoff while retaining CPU geometry needed for mesh shaders, picking, baking, and BLAS.
Objects, materials/textures, lights, decals, water/environment, foliage/wind, coordinates/sublevels/portals, voxels/SDF, planetary voxels, sprites, planar reflections, VG, sky/presentation, visibility, and application extensions are mapped.
Custom components and singleton/index payloads have a typed, closed extension boundary. Raw World, GPU store, built-in buffers, and phase hooks are inaccessible through high-level Scene.
